#: Implementation.md:1
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr "実装"

#: Implementation.md:3
msgid ""
"Small disclaimer: the code I am presenting here is a simplified version of "
"the actual code that is available as an example implementation in this "
"[repository](https://github.com/Iximiel/cudaOnPlumed). However for "
"production runs I would suggest to use the version that are hosted in the "
"main plumed repository, at time of writing this in version "
"[v2.10](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/v2.10/plugins/cudaCoord) or "
"the more updated version in "
"[master](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord) "
"these versions depend on C++17. The actual implementation has type templates"
" and supports pbcs. These particulars are not useful in understanding the "
"basis for a plumed implementation of a simple CV."
msgstr ""
"注：ここでは [リポジトリ](https://github.com/Iximiel/cudaOnPlumed) の例を簡略化しています。本計算には "
"PLUMED 本体の "
"[v2.10](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/v2.10/plugins/cudaCoord) "
"または最新の "
"[master](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord) "
"を推奨します。C++17 が必要です。実装には型 Template と PBC 対応がありますが、簡単な CV の基礎理解には不要なため省きます。"

#: Implementation.md:14
msgid ""
"If this is not the first time you read this I have updated the code on the "
"repository to use the NVIDIA's [CCCL](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl) API. "
"You may find some changes in the code. The code changes are not radical and "
"I may have missed something while updating the page, always refer to the "
"code present in the main [plumed "
"repository](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord)"
" for an up-to-date code."
msgstr ""
"以前読んだ方へ：NVIDIA [CCCL](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl) API "
"を使うよう更新しました。変更は大規模ではありませんが、ページ更新に漏れがあるかもしれません。最新コードは常に [PLUMED "
"本体](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/tree/master/plugins/cudaCoord) "
"を参照してください。"

#: Implementation.md:21 Implementation.md:152
msgid "The switching function"
msgstr "Switching Function"

#: Implementation.md:22
msgid ""
"In this case the coordination is calculated with $\\frac{1}{2} "
"\\sum_{i\\lt{}nat}^{i} \\sum_{j\\lt{}nat,j\\neq i}^{j} f(d_{ij})$, where "
"$d_{ij}$ is the distances between atom $i$ and $j$, and $f(x)$ is a function"
" that usually has the form"
msgstr ""
"Coordination は $\\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i\\lt{}nat}^{i} \\sum_{j\\lt{}nat,j\\neq"
" i}^{j} f(d_{ij})$ で計算します。$d_{ij}$ は原子 $i$ と $j$ の距離で、$f(x)$ は通常、"

#: Implementation.md:35
msgid ""
"and $s(x)$ is a switching function that links smoothly 1 to 0 between $d_0$ "
"and $d_{max}$"
msgstr "$s(x)$ は $d_0$〜$d_{max}$ で1から0を滑らかにつなぐ Switching Function です。"

#: Implementation.md:37
msgid ""
"In this case, I used the RATIONAL function like in the default Plumed "
"implementation: $s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 "
"}\\right)^{n} }{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$."
msgstr ""
"既定の PLUMED と同じ RATIONAL、$s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 "
"}\\right)^{n} }{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r - d_0 }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$ を使います。"

#: Implementation.md:40
msgid ""
"But in this case, for simplicity, the implementation that I am showing will "
"not use the parameter $d_0$, so $s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 "
"}\\right)^{n} }{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$."
msgstr ""
"ただし簡単のため $d_0$ を使わず、$s(r)=\\frac{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)^{n} "
"}{ 1 - \\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)^{m} }$ とします。"

#: Implementation.md:44
msgid ""
"Like in standard plumed implementation, the switching has a stretch "
"parameter: if $s(d_{max}) = shift $ and "
"$stretch=\\frac{1}{s(0)-s(d_{max})}$, $s(x)$ becomes "
"$s^s(x)=s(x)*stretch+shift$"
msgstr ""
"標準実装と同じ Stretch パラメータがあり、$s(d_{max}) = shift "
"$、$stretch=\\frac{1}{s(0)-s(d_{max})}$ なら、$s(x)$ は "
"$s^s(x)=s(x)*stretch+shift$ になります。"

#: Implementation.md:48
msgid "The kernel and the \\_\\_device\\_\\_ functions"
msgstr "Kernel と \\_\\_device\\_\\_ 関数"

#: Implementation.md:49
msgid "The coord kernel"
msgstr "coord Kernel"

#: Implementation.md:51
msgid ""
"In the following code snippets, the comments help read the flow of the code."
" Here the code is presented in a simplified way, without templates for type "
"and without the pbc calculations."
msgstr "以下のコメントで流れを説明します。簡略化し、型 Template と PBC 計算を省いています。"

#: Implementation.md:55
msgid ""
"The simplest kernel for calculating the coordination in a group of atoms is:"
msgstr "原子群の Coordination を計算する最も単純な Kernel は、"

#: Implementation.md:134
msgid ""
"You can view this kernel as the inner body of the nested for loop that can "
"be used to write the most naive serial implementation of the coordination "
"(the outer loop would run on the `i` variable)."
msgstr "これは、単純な逐次実装の二重 For Loop の内側に相当します。外側は `i` で回ります。"

#: Implementation.md:138
msgid ""
"The use of global memory should be limited in a kernel, because accessing "
"global memory is far slower than working on shared memory (that it is not "
"used in this case, shared memory is shared between kernels within a group) "
"or the variables, (the \"local memory\") declared within each kernel."
msgstr ""
"Kernel では Global Memory の使用を抑えます。Shared Memory（この例では未使用）や、Kernel "
"内で宣言した変数（Local Memory）より大幅に遅いためです。Shared Memory は Group 内で共有されます。"

#: Implementation.md:143
msgid ""
"Here within each kernel, I have accumulated the values in local variables "
"and not on the global memory and then update the global memory only at the "
"end of the calculation. Using `mycoord += coord;` instead of `ncoordOut[i] "
"+= coord;` within the loop will speed up the calculations."
msgstr ""
"Local 変数に蓄積し、最後だけ Global を更新します。Loop 内で `ncoordOut[i] += coord;` の代わりに "
"`mycoord += coord;` を使うと高速化できます。"

#: Implementation.md:148
msgid ""
"In the actual implementation the `float myVirial[9];` and `float d[3];` are "
"presented as a collection of 9 and 3 single declared values to use the "
"registers of the kernels, here are declared as an array for clarity."
msgstr ""
"実装では Register を使うため `float myVirial[9];`、`float d[3];` "
"を9個・3個の個別変数にしていますが、ここでは読みやすく Array にしました。"

#: Implementation.md:154
msgid ""
"The switching parameters are stored in a simple struct: when called, kernels"
" accept struct variables as inputs, making it simpler to pass parameters to "
"functions:"
msgstr ""
"Switching パラメータは単純な Struct に格納します。Kernel は Struct を入力に取れ、パラメータを渡しやすくなります。"

#: Implementation.md:167
msgid ""
"`calculateSqr` is a simple interface to the actual switching function and "
"takes the squared distance and prepares it for the actual rational function "
"(by precalculating $\\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)$). It is a rewriting "
"of the `PLMD::SwitchingFunction::calculateSqr` method as a `__device__` "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"`calculateSqr` は距離の二乗を受け、$\\left(\\frac{ r }{ r_0 }\\right)$ を事前計算して "
"Rational 関数に渡す Interface です。`PLMD::SwitchingFunction::calculateSqr` を "
"`__device__` 関数に書き換えたものです。"

#: Implementation.md:192
msgid ""
"Also `pcuda_Rational` is a rewrite to the method "
"`PLMD::SwitchingFunction::do_rational` for the GPU:"
msgstr "`pcuda_Rational` も `PLMD::SwitchingFunction::do_rational` の GPU 版です。"

#: Implementation.md:220
msgid ""
"From what I [understood](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-"
"guide/index.html#noinline-and-forceinline) the compilers tend to inline "
"`__device__` functions. It is possible to enforce the behaviour with "
"`__forceinline__` or `__inline_hint__`"
msgstr ""
"私の [理解](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-"
"guide/index.html#noinline-and-forceinline) では、Compiler は `__device__` を "
"Inline 化する傾向があります。`__forceinline__` または `__inline_hint__` で強制できます。"

#: Implementation.md:225
msgid "Interfacing to cuda: invoking the kernel and the reductions"
msgstr "CUDA Interface：Kernel と Reduction の呼び出し"

#: Implementation.md:226
msgid ""
"This section has changed heavily since the previous version Go to the "
"[helpers](Helpers.md) page for details on the reduction and on how the CCCL "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"この節は以前から大きく変わりました。Reduction と CCCL Interface の詳細は [Helper](Helpers.md) "
"を参照してください。"

#: Implementation.md:230
msgid "Calling the kernel in the calculate() method"
msgstr "calculate() からの Kernel 呼び出し"

#: Implementation.md:232
msgid "As in any other `PLMD::Action` we have a `calculate()` method."
msgstr "ほかの `PLMD::Action` と同様、`calculate()` があります。"

#: Implementation.md:234
msgid ""
"We start with getting the positions of the atoms, and we immediately load "
"them into the GPU:"
msgstr "原子位置を取得し、直ちに GPU に送ります。"

#: Implementation.md:241
msgid ""
"during the construction of the action the number of atoms has already been "
"initialized, so no need to resize `cudaPositions` (for safety reasons "
"`plmdDataToGPU` will do it for you) or `cudaDerivatives`. Moreover, we are "
"using the async version of `plmdDataToGPU`, so we can set up other things on"
" the CPU while the data is copied."
msgstr ""
"Action 構築時に原子数を初期化済みなので、`cudaPositions` や `cudaDerivatives` の Resize "
"は不要です。安全のため `plmdDataToGPU` が実行します。非同期の `plmdDataToGPU` を使うので、Copy 中に CPU "
"で準備できます。"

#: Implementation.md:247
msgid ""
"Then we fetch the number of atoms and we prepare the memory and the number "
"of groups for calling the kernel:"
msgstr "原子数を取得し、Memory と Group 数を準備します。"

#: Implementation.md:260
msgid ""
"`cudaCoordination` and `cudaVirial` are the outputs of the kernel and will "
"need to be reduced after."
msgstr "Kernel 出力の `cudaCoordination` と `cudaVirial` は後で Reduction が必要です。"

#: Implementation.md:263
msgid ""
"the kernel is called with the `<<<>>>` syntax, between the three brackets we"
" specify 2 to 4 information:"
msgstr "`<<<>>>` 内に2〜4項目を指定して Kernel を呼びます。"

#: Implementation.md:265
msgid "the number of groups to use"
msgstr "Group 数。"

#: Implementation.md:266
msgid "the number of threads per group"
msgstr "Group ごとの Thread 数。"

#: Implementation.md:267
msgid "the eventual quantity of shared memory"
msgstr "必要なら Shared Memory 容量。"

#: Implementation.md:268
msgid "the eventual stream to enqueue the kernel into"
msgstr "必要なら Kernel を入れる Stream。"

#: Implementation.md:270
msgid "(specify the shared memory and the stream is optional):"
msgstr "Shared Memory と Stream は任意です。"

#: Implementation.md:281
msgid "Moving the derivatives to the host RAM"
msgstr "微分の Host RAM への転送"

#: Implementation.md:283
msgid ""
"Before moving the data again on the CPU's RAM we want to be sure that the "
"[kernel](#the-coord-kernel) has finished its calculations by calling "
"`cudaDeviceSynchronize();`."
msgstr ""
"CPU RAM に戻す前に、`cudaDeviceSynchronize();` で [Kernel](#the-coord-kernel) "
"の終了を確認します。"

#: Implementation.md:286
msgid "Then we enqueue an async copy of the derivatives."
msgstr "微分の非同期 Copy を Queue に入れます。"

#: Implementation.md:292
msgid "Calling the reductions in the calculate() method"
msgstr "calculate() からの Reduction 呼び出し"

#: Implementation.md:294
msgid ""
"After the [kernel](#the-coord-kernel) finishes we have the virial and the "
"coordination accumulated for each atom: we proceed to accumulate the results"
" for the whole system with the utilities in _cudaHelpers.cuh_, which are "
"written using the building blocks of CCCL/cub. The reduction algorithm is "
"recursively called by the following loop."
msgstr ""
"[Kernel](#the-coord-kernel) 後、各原子の Virial と Coordination を、CCCL/cub を使った "
"_cudaHelpers.cuh_ で全系に集約します。次の Loop で Reduction を再帰的に呼びます。"

#: Implementation.md:341
msgid ""
"The last iteration (where `nGroups == 1`) enqueue the async version of the "
"GPU to CPU copies."
msgstr "最後（`nGroups == 1`）に GPU から CPU への非同期 Copy を Queue に入れます。"

#: Implementation.md:343
msgid ""
"The swaps of the memory are there because the output of an iteration "
"reduction became the input of the next iteration and we want to use the "
"already allocated data as the next result recipient. These swap operations "
"do not move the memory, but should exchange the addresses and the data "
"between the two variables."
msgstr ""
"前の出力が次の入力になるため、確保済み領域を次の出力に再利用するよう Swap します。Memory 自体は移動せず、変数間の Address "
"とデータを交換します。"

#: Implementation.md:348
msgid ""
"The ND-reduction expects the data to be organized as a series of "
"concatenated arrays (this is also known as a block arrangement, at least in "
"the cub manual): `[x0, x1, x2, ..., xn-2, xn-1, y0, y1, y2, ..., yn-2, yn-1,"
" z0,... ]` and so on."
msgstr ""
"ND Reduction は、連結 Array（cub では Block 配置）を期待します：`[x0, x1, x2, ..., xn-2, "
"xn-1, y0, y1, y2, ..., yn-2, yn-1, z0,... ]`。"

#: Implementation.md:352
msgid "Finalizing the results"
msgstr "結果の確定"

#: Implementation.md:354
msgid ""
"After the reduction/accumulation, the data is then uploaded to Plumed with "
"the standard procedure, again we use `cudaDeviceSynchronize();` to be sure "
"that all the data have been moved to the CPU:"
msgstr ""
"集約後、通常の手順で PLUMED に渡します。再び `cudaDeviceSynchronize();` で CPU への転送完了を確認します。"

#: Implementation.md:365
msgid "Other implementations"
msgstr "ほかの実装"

